  "simple_explanation": "This passage is introducing Tim Costello and explaining why he cares so much about poverty.\n\nWhen he was in Year 9, he asked his teacher whether poverty is something that just happens naturally, like the tides or sunrise. He later decided the answer was no: poverty is not natural, it is caused by decisions people make, especially government policies.\n\nThe article describes him sitting on a beach near his home while reflecting on this idea. It says he has spent more than 30 years working to fight poverty in Australia and around the world. He has also been involved in other important work, such as going to war zones and disaster areas, serving as mayor of St Kilda, writing books, and being recognized as an important national figure.\n\nThe text also notes that people often mistake him for his brother, Peter Costello, who is a former Australian treasurer. Tim Costello is known as a Baptist minister and as the former leader of World Vision Australia.",
  "in_plain_language": [
    "Tim Costello has spent most of his life trying to help poor people.",
    "He believes poverty is not something unavoidable; it happens because of human choices and policies.",
    "He has had a very active career in public service, religion, and charity work.",
    "People sometimes confuse him with his brother, Peter Costello."
  ]
}

